UniMemory Rust is an independent Rust implementation of the unified frontend
design from https://github.com/dugan-dev/UniMemory (MIT, copyright dugan-dev).
The original UniMemory repository is not included or modified.

Pinned source dependencies are Git submodules, not copied into the parent Git tree:

allocator-api2 0.4.0
https://github.com/zakarumych/allocator-api2
revision 1644e70ebc31746ca6b20ccf8cf5865c8438238e
MIT OR Apache-2.0; licenses remain in external/allocator-api2.

libmimalloc-sys 0.1.49 / mimalloc v3.3.2
https://github.com/purpleprotocol/mimalloc_rust
revision a35cc759c071fd7bd586685048367839002b95dd
native mimalloc revision 30b2d9d89099bee08e9f67a1ffb3e12e7ba45227
MIT; licenses remain in external/mimalloc-rust and its native submodules.

tikv-jemalloc-sys 0.7.0 / jemalloc 5.3.1
https://github.com/tikv/jemallocator
revision 0e9129157d261cf6bda86d5dcd9eba94f3cd0f96
native jemalloc revision 81034ce1f1373e37dc865038e1bc8eeecf559ce8
MIT/Apache-2.0 wrapper; native jemalloc BSD-2-Clause. Licenses remain in submodules.
Windows MSVC uses a separately built prefixed jemalloc SDK; no SDK binaries are
committed. Redistribution of such binaries must retain the selected SDK notices.

The Standard backend uses only the Rust standard library allocator; no C++ bridge
is compiled. The cc crate is a transitive build dependency of libmimalloc-sys and
tikv-jemalloc-sys, MIT OR Apache-2.0. Cargo.lock fixes the resolved build-tool
dependencies. Optional chart generation uses matplotlib.
